        <li><strong>Capacitors degrade from extreme summer heat:</strong> The ceiling fan motor capacitor provides the phase shift required for starting torque and high speed. Indian summers and grid voltage fluctuations degrade the internal dielectric oil/film, leaving the fan spinning at half speed or requiring a manual push to start.</li>
